Below is a raw load-balancer access log (8 lines), single-line JSON per entry:
{"ts":"10:00:01","status":200,"bytes":504}
{"ts":"10:00:02","status":504,"bytes":812}
{"ts":"10:00:03","status":500,"bytes":230}
{"ts":"10:00:04","status":504,"bytes":91}
{"ts":"10:00:05","status":504,"bytes":6}
{"ts":"10:00:06","status":200,"bytes":150}
{"ts":"10:00:07","status":503,"bytes":504}
{"ts":"10:00:08","status":504,"bytes":78}
Count lines containing "status":504, ignoring 504 when it appears only in bytes. The final summary must state one integer: the count.

Compare these two raw nginx snippets exactly as written:
VERSION A:
listen 8080;
server_name api.internal;
proxy_pass http://backend;
timeout 30s;
VERSION B:
listen 8080;
server_name api.internal;
proxy_pass http://backend-v2;
timeout 30s;
keepalive 15s;
Identify every line that was changed or added between A and B, quoting the exact old and new text for changes. Do not summarize the intent of the change. The final summary must list each difference as (line role, old text, new text).
